  "prefLabel": "Env-Wt 102.44 Crib",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Wt 102.44 “Crib” means an enclosure or framework of durable material, such as timber or prefabricated concrete, that is securely fastened together and filled with an inert ballast, such as stone, that typically is used to support a docking structure in the water.\n\nSource. (See Revision Notes #1, #2, #3, and #4 at Chapter heading for Env-Wt 100) #12801, eff 12-15-19; renumbered by #13945 (formerly Env-Wt 102.45)",
